1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,000
Browser agents look reliable when we test whether they work once.
AgentGauntlet tests whether they survive production.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Same task. Same agent. Four environments.
Real Solari cloud browsers.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Baseline passes in 7 steps. Then the session expires
mid-task — and the agent fails.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
This one passed. It also went from 7 steps to 19.
A pass/fail benchmark records that as identical to baseline.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
We never trust the agent saying it's done. The evaluator reads
the benchmark site's server-side state, which the agent can't fake.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Every failure is classified from evidence —
this one is an auth failure the agent never recovered from.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Bring your own agent. Your repository runs inside an isolated
Solari Sandbox, with a scoped browser endpoint — never the account key.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,800
Four runs is a demonstration, not a benchmark —
and the product shows the confidence interval to prove it.
